IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part VI, the rest of "Enforcement": privilege (s 129), default (s 130), questions that
-- arise in legal proceedings (ss 131 and 132) and evidence of documents (s 134); ss 133 is repealed. Piece ei4. Layer 1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
--
-- Conventions as in ei4-part-vi-review.l4. In addition:
--   * A duty on a court is a BOOLEAN that is TRUE while the duty applies; the fact that ends it (a ruling or decision received) is an input.
--   * A provision on evidence is a BOOLEAN that is TRUE when the document has the effect the text gives it; FALSE means this section
--     does not give it that effect.
-- Hohfeld, for these sections: the privilege in s 129 is the immunity of the person who speaks to the Commission, and the no-right of anyone
-- who might sue for defamation; the Commission's power to pay despite a default (s 130) is the claimant's no-right to be paid (the section
-- says "may"); the court's duties in ss 131 and 132 are the parties' claims that the question be decided by the proper decision-maker first.

§ `Part VI -- Enforcement, continued`

§§ `s 129 Privilege`

-- src:1970 | 129 When an employer, claimant or other person gives the Commission written, oral or documentary evidence required for the proper determination of the entitlement of a claimant to benefits, the giving of the evidence is an occasion of qualified privilege.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 129 (src:1970)
GIVEN `gives the Commission the evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is written, oral or documentary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the evidence is required for the proper determination of the entitlement of a claimant to benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 129 the giving of the evidence is an occasion of qualified privilege` IF
        `gives the Commission the evidence`
    AND `the evidence is written, oral or documentary`
    AND `the evidence is required for the proper determination of the entitlement of a claimant to benefits`

§§ `s 130 Default`

-- "another person": read literally, the person who loses the right is not the person whose failure or neglect caused the loss (fork F-ei4-10).
-- src:1972 | 130 If, because of the failure or neglect of any person to comply with this Act or the regulations, another person loses the right to claim, in whole or in part, any benefits to which the person would otherwise be entitled, the Commission may nevertheless pay the benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 130 (src:1972)
GIVEN `a person failed or neglected to comply with this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `because of that failure or neglect another person loses the right to claim, in whole or in part, benefits to which that other person would otherwise be entitled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 130 the Commission may nevertheless pay the benefits` IF
        `a person failed or neglected to comply with this Act or the regulations`
    AND `because of that failure or neglect another person loses the right to claim, in whole or in part, benefits to which that other person would otherwise be entitled`

§§ `s 131 Question under section 90`

-- src:1974 | 131 (1) If a question specified in section 90 arises in any legal proceedings, the justice, judge or court before whom it arises shall
-- src:1975 | (a) refer the question to an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency under that section and defer further proceedings until the officer’s ruling is received, if the question has not been decided by the authorized officer; and
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 131(1)(a) (src:1974-1975)
GIVEN `a question specified in section 90 arises in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 90 (piece ei3)
      `the question has been decided by the authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 131(1)(a) the court must refer the question to an authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency and defer further proceedings until the ruling is received` IF
        `a question specified in section 90 arises in legal proceedings`
    AND NOT (`the question has been decided by the authorized officer of the Canada Revenue Agency`)

-- src:1976 | (b) on receipt of the ruling, proceed with the hearing and judgment of the legal proceedings.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 131(1)(b) (src:1976)
GIVEN `a question specified in section 90 arose in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has received the ruling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 131(1)(b) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` IF
        `a question specified in section 90 arose in legal proceedings`
    AND `the court has received the ruling`

-- src:1978 | (2) If an appeal has been made under section 91 or 103, the justice, judge or court shall defer judgment until
-- src:1979 | (a) a decision of the Minister of National Revenue is received, in the case of an appeal under section 91; or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 131(2)(a) (src:1978-1979)
GIVEN `an appeal has been made under section 91` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 91 (piece ei3)
      `the decision of the Minister of National Revenue has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 131(2)(a) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Minister of National Revenue is received` IF
        `an appeal has been made under section 91`
    AND NOT (`the decision of the Minister of National Revenue has been received`)

-- src:1978 | (2) If an appeal has been made under section 91 or 103, the justice, judge or court shall defer judgment until
-- src:1980 | (b) a decision of the Tax Court of Canada is received, in the case of an appeal under section 103.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 131(2)(b) (src:1978) (src:1980)
GIVEN `an appeal has been made under section 103` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 103 (piece ei3)
      `the decision of the Tax Court of Canada has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 131(2)(b) the court must defer judgment until the decision of the Tax Court of Canada is received` IF
        `an appeal has been made under section 103`
    AND NOT (`the decision of the Tax Court of Canada has been received`)

§§ `s 132 Question for Commission`

-- src:1982 | 132 (1) If a question that could be decided by the Commission arises in any legal proceedings, the justice, judge or court before whom the question arises shall refer the question to the Commission and defer further proceedings until the Commission’s decision is received.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 132(1) (src:1982)
GIVEN `a question that could be decided by the Commission arises in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission's decision has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 132(1) the court must refer the question to the Commission and defer further proceedings until the Commission's decision is received` IF
        `a question that could be decided by the Commission arises in legal proceedings`
    AND NOT (`the Commission's decision has been received`)

-- src:1984 | (2) If an appeal from a decision of the Commission, or a person authorized by the Commission, is pending on the question arising in any legal proceedings, the justice, judge or court before whom the question arises shall defer further proceedings until the appeal decision is received.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 132(2) (src:1984)
GIVEN `an appeal from a decision of the Commission, or a person authorized by the Commission, is pending on the question arising in legal proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appeal decision has been received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 132(2) the court must defer further proceedings until the appeal decision is received` IF
        `an appeal from a decision of the Commission, or a person authorized by the Commission, is pending on the question arising in legal proceedings`
    AND NOT (`the appeal decision has been received`)

-- src:1986 | (3) On receipt of the decision, the justice, judge or court shall proceed with the hearing and judgment and, in any proceedings under this Act, the decision is conclusive except in accordance with the Federal Courts Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 132(3) (src:1986)
GIVEN `the court has received the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 132(3) the court must proceed with the hearing and judgment` IF
    `the court has received the decision`

-- "except in accordance with the Federal Courts Act": the decision is open to challenge only by the route that Act provides.
-- src:1986 | (3) On receipt of the decision, the justice, judge or court shall proceed with the hearing and judgment and, in any proceedings under this Act, the decision is conclusive except in accordance with the Federal Courts Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 132(3) (src:1986)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is challenged in accordance with the Federal Courts Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 132(3) the decision is conclusive` IF
        `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act`
    AND NOT (`the decision is challenged in accordance with the Federal Courts Act`)

§§ `s 133 Repealed`

-- src:1987 | 133 [Repealed, 2015, c. 13, s. 54]
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 133 (src:1987)
`s 133 repealed, and therefore not encoded` MEANS
        "133 [Repealed, 2015, c. 13, s. 54]"

§§ `s 134 Evidence of documents, etc.`

-- Paragraphs (a) to (d) of subsection (1), each a kind of document; the text then gives all four the same effect.
-- src:1990 | (a) a document appearing to be a resolution, record or other proceeding of the Commission or other proceeding under this Act or a copy of it, and appearing to be certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary of the Commission,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(1)(a) (src:1990)
GIVEN `appears to be a resolution, record or other proceeding of the Commission or other proceeding under this Act, or a copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appears to be certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary of the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(1)(a) the document is a resolution, record or proceeding certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary of the Commission` IF
        `appears to be a resolution, record or other proceeding of the Commission or other proceeding under this Act, or a copy of it`
    AND `appears to be certified by a Commissioner or the Secretary of the Commission`

-- src:1991 | (b) a document appearing to be, or appearing to be a copy of or extract from,
-- src:1992 | (i) a document in the custody of the Commission or a document issued under this Act, or
-- src:1993 | (ii) an entry in any books or records in the custody of the Commission,
-- src:1994 | and appearing to be certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(1)(b) (src:1991-1994)
GIVEN `appears to be, or to be a copy of or extract from, a document in the custody of the Commission or a document issued under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appears to be, or to be a copy of or extract from, an entry in any books or records in the custody of the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appears to be certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(1)(b) the document is a document or entry certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` IF
        (   `appears to be, or to be a copy of or extract from, a document in the custody of the Commission or a document issued under this Act`
         OR `appears to be, or to be a copy of or extract from, an entry in any books or records in the custody of the Commission`)
    AND `appears to be certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act`

-- src:1995 | (c) a document appearing to be certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act and stating the amount of any contributions paid, payable or owing or the amount of any benefits or other amount paid to or owing by any person, or
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(1)(c) (src:1995)
GIVEN `appears to be certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `states the amount of any contributions paid, payable or owing or the amount of any benefits or other amount paid to or owing by any person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(1)(c) the document is a certified statement of an amount paid, payable or owing` IF
        `appears to be certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act`
    AND `states the amount of any contributions paid, payable or owing or the amount of any benefits or other amount paid to or owing by any person`

-- src:1996 | (d) a document appearing
-- src:1997 | (i) to be, or to be a copy of or extract from, any of the following, namely, an employer’s register, books, pay sheets, records of wages, ledgers, accounts or other documents, and
-- src:1998 | (ii) to be certified by an inspector or other person employed in the administration of this Act to whom the documents mentioned in subparagraph (i) were produced under this Act,
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(1)(d) (src:1996-1998)
GIVEN `appears to be, or to be a copy of or extract from, an employer's register, books, pay sheets, records of wages, ledgers, accounts or other documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `appears to be certified by an inspector or other person employed in the administration of this Act to whom the documents were produced under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(1)(d) the document is a copy or extract of an employer's records certified by an inspector or other person employed in the administration of this Act` IF
        `appears to be, or to be a copy of or extract from, an employer's register, books, pay sheets, records of wages, ledgers, accounts or other documents`
    AND `appears to be certified by an inspector or other person employed in the administration of this Act to whom the documents were produced under this Act`

-- src:1989 | 134 (1) In any proceedings under this Act,
-- src:1999 | is evidence of the facts appearing in the document without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(1) (src:1989) (src:1999)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is within paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is within paragraph (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is within paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is within paragraph (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(1) the document is evidence of the facts appearing in it without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate and without further proof` IF
        `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act`
    AND (   `the document is within paragraph (a)`
         OR `the document is within paragraph (b)`
         OR `the document is within paragraph (c)`
         OR `the document is within paragraph (d)`)

-- src:2001 | (2) For the purposes of this Act and the regulations and any proceedings under them, a document appearing to be a certificate of the Commission or a person authorized by the Commission to the effect that a notice, request, demand or other document was sent by mail is evidence that the notice, request, demand or other document was received by the addressee in the ordinary course of the mails.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(2) (src:2001)
GIVEN `the document appears to be a certificate of the Commission or a person authorized by the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate is to the effect that a notice, request, demand or other document was sent by mail` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(2) the certificate is evidence that the notice, request, demand or other document was received by the addressee in the ordinary course of the mails` IF
        `the document appears to be a certificate of the Commission or a person authorized by the Commission`
    AND `the certificate is to the effect that a notice, request, demand or other document was sent by mail`

-- src:2003 | (3) In any proceedings under this Act or the regulations, a print that is
-- src:2004 | (a) made from a photographic film or from a document in electronic form made by the Commission for the purpose of keeping a permanent record of a document, and
-- src:2005 | (b) certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act
-- src:2006 | is admissible in evidence for all purposes for which the recorded document would be admitted as evidence in the proceedings without proof of the signature or official character of the person appearing to have signed the certificate.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(3) (src:2003-2006)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the print is made from a photographic film or from a document in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the film or electronic document was made by the Commission for the purpose of keeping a permanent record of a document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the print is certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(3) the print is admissible in evidence for all purposes for which the recorded document would be admitted` IF
        `the proceedings are proceedings under this Act or the regulations`
    AND `the print is made from a photographic film or from a document in electronic form`
    AND `the film or electronic document was made by the Commission for the purpose of keeping a permanent record of a document`
    AND `the print is certified by the Commission or a person employed in the administration of this Act`

-- "For greater certainty": an electronic document is a document for every reference to a document in section 134.
-- src:2008 | (4) For greater certainty, a reference to a document in this section includes a document in electronic form.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 134(4) (src:2008)
GIVEN `is a document in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a document in any other form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 134(4) the thing is a document for the purposes of section 134` IF
       `is a document in electronic form`
    OR `is a document in any other form`
